## Getting Started

1) Clone this repo and review the baseline documents under `docs/`.
2) Select cloud provider(s) and IaC tool (Terraform/Pulumi). See `docs/infrastructure/`.
3) Stand up dev environment and landing zone. Implement IAM, logging, and secrets management first.
4) Configure data platform (lakehouse) and governance. Add ingestion connectors for core systems.
5) Establish AI/ML platform guardrails and evaluation harness before deploying pilot copilots.
6) Tailor compliance policies to jurisdictions (e.g., SEC, FCA, MAS). Engage counsel for review.

## Execution Roadmap (90-Day Sprint)

- Week 1–2: Landing zone, IAM, secrets, SIEM, baseline policies, vendor inventory
- Week 3–4: Data lakehouse and catalog, PII classification, DLP, ingestion MVP
- Week 5–6: Model registry, eval harness, prompt safety, RAI controls, pilot copilots
- Week 7–8: Client onboarding workflow, CRM schema, reporting pipeline, portal stub
- Week 9–10: OMS/EMS connectivity plan, reconciliation design, valuation policy finalization
- Week 11–12: DR/BCP tests, tabletop IR, SOC2 roadmap, automated evidence collection

## Compliance Readiness

- Code of Ethics, P&P manual, AML/KYC, trade surveillance, conflicts of interest
- Personal trading, gifts/entertainment, outside business activities tracking
- Business continuity and incident response playbooks with RTO/RPO objectives

## Security Principles

- Zero trust: strong identity, device posture, least privilege, short-lived creds
- Secrets: centralized KMS/HSM, automatic rotation, no plaintext in repos
- Data protection: tokenization, row/column permissions, differential privacy where appropriate

## Data Platform

- Lakehouse with medallion architecture (bronze/silver/gold)
- Catalog + lineage (e.g., Unity, DataHub, OpenMetadata)
- Quality SLAs and automated checks; retention and legal hold

## AI/ML Platform

- Model registry and evaluation gates; red-teaming and safety tests
- Governance: dataset cards, model cards, usage policies, human-in-the-loop
- Retrieval strategy patterns, privacy-preserving analytics, and audit logging

## Client and Ops

- CRM schema, onboarding workflow, KYC collection, e-sign integration
- Reporting: client portal baseline, periodic statements, ad-hoc insights
- Ops: reconciliation, cash management, fees, valuation controls

## Contributing

Use issues and PRs to propose improvements. All contributions must pass linting and security checks.
